<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves rise to $1.742 bln on Oct 4.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves rise to $1.742 bln on Oct 4.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Friday its net international reserves stood at $1.742 billion on October 4, up $52 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In the previous week to September 30, international reserves grew $164 million.</p>
<p>The Central Bank gave no reason for the growth in reserves.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $1.556 billion.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
</text>
